---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
---
<Layout
  title="About — Param Dave"
  description="Param Dave is a research-minded ML engineer and product builder who connects business KPIs to model behavior and shipped AI systems."
>
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-5xl px-6 pt-16 pb-12 sm:pt-20">
    <p class="font-mono text-xs tracking-widest text-amber-600 uppercase dark:text-amber-400">
      About
    </p>
    <h1 class="mt-3 max-w-3xl text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight sm:text-5xl">
      I connect business outcomes to model behavior—and build the system in between.
    </h1>
    <div class="mt-8 grid gap-8 lg:grid-cols-[1.2fr_0.8fr] lg:gap-14">
      <div class="space-y-5 text-neutral-700 dark:text-neutral-300">
        <p>
          I'm a Senior Machine Learning Engineer at TRC Inc, working remotely from India.
          I build agentic AI systems, evaluation frameworks, and document-intelligence
          pipelines where plausible output is not enough—the system has to be measurable,
          diagnosable, and reliable inside a real workflow. I work backward from the KPI,
          translate it into technical requirements, and own the path through application delivery.
        </p>
        <p>
          My route here ran through robotics, computer vision, and 3D perception: SfM at
          scale, Gaussian Splatting for real-time rendering, and LiDAR segmentation for
          utility infrastructure. That work taught me that reproducing a paper is only the
          beginning. Data quality, runtime, evaluation design, and deployment constraints
          often contain the harder research questions.
        </p>
        <p>
          Today I apply the same mindset to LLM systems. I move across abstraction layers:
          business outcome, user workflow, application behavior, system evaluation, and
          model training. Production failures shape the questions I investigate; experiments
          shape what I ship next.
        </p>
      </div>

      <aside class="rounded-xl border border-neutral-200 p-5 dark:border-neutral-800">
        <p class="font-mono text-[10px] tracking-widest text-neutral-500 uppercase">Current coordinates</p>
        <dl class="mt-4 space-y-4 text-sm">
          <div>
            <dt class="text-neutral-500">Role</dt>
            <dd class="mt-1 font-medium">Senior Machine Learning Engineer</dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt class="text-neutral-500">Based in</dt>
            <dd class="mt-1 font-medium">India · working remotely</dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt class="text-neutral-500">Current focus</dt>
            <dd class="mt-1 font-medium">Reliable agents, evaluation, and inference</dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt class="text-neutral-500">Operating range</dt>
            <dd class="mt-1 font-medium">Business KPI → application → model → evaluation</dd>
          </div>
        </dl>
      </aside>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
      <a
        href={`${base}/experience`}
        class="rounded-md bg-neutral-900 px-4 py-2 text-sm font-medium text-white hover:bg-neutral-700 dark:bg-amber-400 dark:text-neutral-900 dark:hover:bg-amber-300"
      >
        Full experience →
      </a>
      <a
        href={`${base}/skills`}
        class="rounded-md border border-neutral-300 px-4 py-2 text-sm font-medium hover:border-neutral-500 dark:border-neutral-700 dark:hover:border-neutral-500"
      >
        Technical toolkit
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="border-y border-neutral-200 dark:border-neutral-800">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl px-6 py-14">
      <p class="font-mono text-xs tracking-widest text-neutral-500 uppercase">Working principles</p>
      <div class="mt-6 grid gap-5 md:grid-cols-3">
        <article>
          <h2 class="text-base font-semibold">Start with the outcome</h2>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-400">
            A model is useful when it improves a workflow or KPI. That outcome defines
            which technical uncertainty is worth reducing.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <h2 class="text-base font-semibold">Translate across layers</h2>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-400">
            Turn a business goal into product behavior, evaluation targets, and focused
            data or model experiments without losing the original intent.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <h2 class="text-base font-semibold">Own the full loop</h2>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-400">
            Research, application engineering, and deployment belong in one feedback loop.
            Shipping reveals what the clean experiment missed.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mx-auto max-w-5xl px-6 py-14">
    <div class="grid gap-12 md:grid-cols-2">
      <div>
        <h2 class="font-mono text-xs tracking-widest text-neutral-500 uppercase">Education</h2>
        <div class="mt-6 space-y-6">
          <div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-4">
            <div>
              <h3 class="text-base font-semibold">M.E. Robotics</h3>
              <p class="text-sm text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-400">University of Maryland, College Park</p>
            </div>
            <span class="shrink-0 font-mono text-xs text-neutral-500">2023</span>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3 class="text-base font-semibold">B.E. Mechanical Engineering</h3>
            <p class="text-sm text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-400">Nirma University, India</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="font-mono text-xs tracking-widest text-neutral-500 uppercase">Beyond work</h2>
        <p class="mt-6 text-sm leading-relaxed text-neutral-700 dark:text-neutral-300">
          Hiking is my reset button. I also follow markets closely and read across
          financial history, geopolitics, philosophy, and how businesses operate beneath
          their investor decks. When I am not reading, I lift or play football, cricket,
          badminton, and tennis.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="border-t border-neutral-200 dark:border-neutral-800">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl px-6 py-14">
      <h2 class="font-mono text-xs tracking-widest text-neutral-500 uppercase">Get in touch</h2>
      <dl class="mt-6 grid gap-5 text-sm sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4">
        <div>
          <dt class="text-neutral-500">Email</dt>
          <dd class="mt-1">
            <a href="mailto:param10.dave@gmail.com" class="font-medium hover:text-amber-600 dark:hover:text-amber-400">
              Write to me
            </a>
          </dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt class="text-neutral-500">LinkedIn</dt>
          <dd class="mt-1">
            <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/param-dave-823910136/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="font-medium hover:text-amber-600 dark:hover:text-amber-400">
              /in/param-dave ↗
            </a>
          </dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt class="text-neutral-500">GitHub</dt>
          <dd class="mt-1">
            <a href="https://github.com/ParamDave5" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="font-medium hover:text-amber-600 dark:hover:text-amber-400">
              @ParamDave5 ↗
            </a>
          </dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt class="text-neutral-500">Résumé</dt>
          <dd class="mt-1">
            <a href="https://drive.google.com/file/d/15KrFphCU_7DVGiPR1wP2tHohGw3woHly/view?usp=sharing" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="font-medium hover:text-amber-600 dark:hover:text-amber-400">
              View résumé ↗
            </a>
          </dd>
        </div>
      </dl>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
